.TH PATH_NORMALIZE 3
.SH NAME
path_normalize, path_normalize2 \- normalize a filesystem path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t path_normalize(char* " path ");"
.PP
.BI "size_t path_normalize2(char* " path ", size_t " nb ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_normalize
and
.B path_normalize2
modify the provided
.I path
in-place to create a canonical, normalized form.
.PP
Normalization removes redundant elements from the path string:
.TP
.B Redundant separators
Consecutive path separators (e.g., "//") are collapsed into a single separator.
.TP
.B Current directory references
Elements equivalent to "." are removed.
.TP
.B Parent directory references
Elements equivalent to ".." are resolved by removing the preceding path component, provided the path structure permits.
.PP
.B path_normalize
assumes
.I path
is a null-terminated string.
.B path_normalize2
operates on a buffer of size
.I nb
and does not rely on null-termination.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the length of the resulting normalized string in bytes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_append (3)